# ----------------------------------------------- scratch from the asset scripts
# scripts/build-hero-poster.sh and build-og-image.sh work in temp dirs, but these
# turn up if a stage is run by hand.
.imgwork/
.ogcheck.png
*.tmp

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, even though they are generated:
#
#   public/hero-greeting-poster.webp   built by scripts/build-hero-poster.sh
#   public/og-default.jpg              built by scripts/build-og-image.sh
#   public/ntaka-mark.webp             built by scripts/build-logo-assets.sh
#   public/ntaka-mark-512.png          "
#   public/apple-touch-icon.png        "
#   public/favicon.ico, favicon-32.png "
#   public/flags/*.svg                 vendored from lipis/flag-icons (MIT)
#   art/                               the original source artwork (logo + hero photo)
#
# All three scripts need ImageMagick 7, which a CI runner usually will not have, so the
# outputs are committed and the scripts exist to reproduce them.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
